        "node_id": "n_7_ea3b04",
        "thought_text": "The current approach using a greedy method to construct the optimal reconstruction by always choosing the fragment with the longest overlap at each step may not always lead to the correct solution, especially when there are multiple valid paths. Instead, we should use a more comprehensive approach that considers all possible sequences of overlapping fragments and selects the one with the maximum length. This method will ensure we find the optimal reconstruction if it exists, and correctly identify when there are multiple valid reconstructions or when no valid reconstruction is possible.",
