      "rev_n_6_0c6c8c_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_6_0c6c8c_1",
        "node_id": "n_6_0c6c8c",
        "thought_text": "The current approach using a greedy algorithm with backtracking may not always find the optimal reconstruction due to its local nature. A more robust solution would be to use a dynamic programming approach combined with backtracking. This would allow us to consider all possible combinations of fragments while efficiently storing and reusing intermediate results. This approach would help avoid the issue of missing the optimal sequence that starts with a fragment that wasn't initially considered as a starting point in the greedy algorithm.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5742887502876773740",
